WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.767
Transformer models are powerful statistical models, not automatic sources of truth.

00:00:05.767 --> 00:00:11.037
A generative model can produce fluent text that is unsupported or incorrect.

00:00:11.037 --> 00:00:18.182
A pretrained checkpoint may not know recent information, private documents,

00:00:18.182 --> 00:00:18.932
or facts outside its training data.

00:00:18.932 --> 00:00:25.867
Context windows limit how much evidence can be supplied at one time.

00:00:25.867 --> 00:00:30.932
Training data can introduce bias or uneven performance across languages, domains, and populations.

00:00:30.932 --> 00:00:37.642
Large models also create cost, latency, energy, and deployment challenges.

00:00:37.642 --> 00:00:41.997
The practical response is not to avoid the technology entirely;

00:00:41.997 --> 00:00:46.327
it is to design evaluation and verification around the task.

00:00:46.327 --> 00:00:50.472
For classification, inspect errors by class.

00:00:50.472 --> 00:00:54.662
For retrieval, measure whether relevant documents are found.

00:00:54.662 --> 00:00:58.282
For generation, check claims against evidence.

00:00:58.282 --> 00:01:04.497
For high-stakes applications, include appropriate human review and domain expertise.

00:01:04.497 --> 00:01:09.688
Good model use combines capability with explicit limits and validation.
